{"name":"Cognac","hex":"#d48c46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cognac","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city and commune of Charente department, region of Nouvelle-Aquitaine, France; famous for cognac brandy.","Alternative letter-case form of cognac (brandy from Cognac)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cognac"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cognac","blocks":[{"text":"Cognac is a variety of brandy named after the commune of Cognac, France. It is produced in the surrounding departments of Charente and Charente-Maritime, in an officially designated wine-growing region. This region is divided into six districts with different cognacs produced in each."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Cognac_glass.jpg/330px-Cognac_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cognac","wikidata":"Q284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Cognac_glass_-_tulip_shaped.JPG/500px-Cognac_glass_-_tulip_shaped.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Cognac_glass_-_tulip_shaped.JPG/500px-Cognac_glass_-_tulip_shaped.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cognac in a tulip glass","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACognac_glass_-_tulip_shaped.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Cognac_pot_still_-_20091205.jpg/500px-Cognac_pot_still_-_20091205.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Cognac_pot_still_-_20091205.jpg/1280px-Cognac_pot_still_-_20091205.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Cognac_pot_still_-_2009120